WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.710
In 2013, Spain's unemployment
rate for people under 25

2
00:00:04.710 --> 00:00:06.990
was above 50 per cent.

3
00:00:06.990 --> 00:00:10.870
So did half of all young
people in Spain have no job?

4
00:00:10.870 --> 00:00:13.920
Not quite. Some young people are counted.

5
00:00:13.920 --> 00:00:16.140
Some are not counted at all.

6
00:00:16.140 --> 00:00:17.930
So who counts as unemployed,

7
00:00:17.930 --> 00:00:20.270
and who slips through the count?

8
00:00:20.270 --> 00:00:23.040
In this mission, you'll
split a whole population into

9
00:00:23.040 --> 00:00:26.890
three groups and calculate the
unemployment rate yourself.

10
00:00:26.890 --> 00:00:29.820
Then you'll compare two very
different ways of counting

11
00:00:29.820 --> 00:00:33.210
people out of work, and
see why they disagree.

12
00:00:33.210 --> 00:00:36.890
Your mission: find out who
the unemployment rate counts,

13
00:00:36.890 --> 00:00:38.190
and who it leaves out.
